 takeaways=['Building docks, boat lifts or seawalls, dredging and filling below the ordinary high-water mark on Great Lakes bottomlands requires an EGLE permit.','Projects that need an EGLE permit on the Great Lakes also need a U.S. Army Corps of Engineers permit. One application through MiEnviro Portal reaches both.','Lake St. Clair’s ordinary high-water mark is 574.7 feet (1955 datum) or 575.3 feet (1985 datum).','Rules vary by site and project. Confirm with EGLE before work starts.'],
